---
import ToolLayout from "../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro";
import { AreaConverter } from "../../../components/converters/AreaConverter.js";
import { getToolByPath } from "../../../content/tools.js";

const tool = getToolByPath("/tools/converters/area")!;
---

<ToolLayout
  tool={tool}
  purpose="Area converter for acres, square feet, square meters, hectares, and square miles."
>
  <AreaConverter client:load />

  <Fragment slot="details">
    <h2>Supported units</h2>
    <p>Every conversion multiplies by the factor below to reach square meters, then divides by the target unit's factor.</p>
    <table>
      <caption>Square meters in one of each unit</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Unit</th>
          <th scope="col">Square meters</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Square millimeter (mm²)</td>
          <td>0.000001</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Square centimeter (cm²)</td>
          <td>0.0001</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Square meter (m²)</td>
          <td>1</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Hectare (ha)</td>
          <td>10,000</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Square kilometer (km²)</td>
          <td>1,000,000</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Square foot (ft²)</td>
          <td>0.09290304</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Square yard (yd²)</td>
          <td>0.83612736</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Acre (ac)</td>
          <td>4,046.8564224</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Square mile (mi²)</td>
          <td>2,589,988.110336</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Every unit is converted through square meters as a common base, then into your target unit, so every
      conversion pair stays mathematically consistent. Distances use the
      <a href="/tools/converters/length">length converter</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      The converter opens on 1 square meter, which it shows as 10.76391 square feet. One acre is exactly 43,560 square
      feet, 4,046.856422 square meters, and 0.404686 hectares at the same six-decimal display. One hectare is 2.471054
      acres at that display.
    </p>

    <h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Conversion factors use standard international definitions (e.g. 1 acre = 4,046.8564224 m² exactly).</li>
      <li>Results are rounded for display; internal calculations retain full floating-point precision.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reference</h2>
    <p>Area conversion factors follow NIST Handbook 44, the standard US reference for weights and measures.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
